// `todo()` is the exception to "a comptime panic is a compile error": it means
// the block hasn't been written yet, and a program full of them still has to
// compile. The const runs at runtime, where the same `todo()` panics.
const D: i64 = comptime { todo("write the table") }

func main() { println(D.to_string()) }
